npm packages — read before publishing
-------------------------------------

The workspace packages are still named `@getpaseo/*`. That scope belongs to
the upstream author: as of 2026-08-02 the published `@getpaseo/cli`,
`@getpaseo/server`, `@getpaseo/relay` and `@getpaseo/highlight` packages are
at 0.2.5 with `boudra` as the sole maintainer.

This fork has never published to that scope and cannot — npm will reject it.
But five packages are missing `"private": true`, so the configuration invites
an attempt that will simply fail:

    @getpaseo/cli
    @getpaseo/expo-two-way-audio
    @getpaseo/highlight
    @getpaseo/relay
    @getpaseo/server

README.md tells users to run `npm install -g @bas-more/cli`. No such package
exists on npm. A rename to a `@bas-more` scope was evidently started in the
documentation and never carried through to package.json, so the install
instruction currently cannot work.

Resolve this one way or the other before any release: either complete the
rename to a scope this project controls, or mark the packages private and
correct the README. Publishing under another author's scope is not an option.


